---
description: Test conventions for this repository
globs: ["tests/**/*.js"]
alwaysApply: false
---

This rule is hand written rather than generated, because glob scoping is something Cursor offers
that the shared AGENTS.md format cannot express, and it only loads when you are editing a test.

- The runner is `node --test`, so never import from jest, vitest, mocha, or chai.
- Assertions come from `node:assert/strict` and tests come from `node:test`.
- Any file that creates tasks must call `resetTasks()` in a `beforeEach` hook, because the store in
  `src/services/tasks.js` is module level state that survives between cases.
- Call `route()` from `src/router.js` directly instead of starting a server, so a case can assert
  on the status and the payload in one object.
